<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Plessey half yr shr little changed, no div.</title>
<headline>Plessey half yr shr little changed, no div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     21.9	  vs 21.6</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   29.51	 vs 26.49</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   36.48	 vs 42.47</p>
<p>    Tax			  7.00	 vs 16.57</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    8.01	 vs received 3.39</p>
<p>    Turnover		 536.46	 vs 466.02</p>
<p>Full name: Plessey Corporation Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said that deliveries of telecommunications orders, seasonally higher turnover in consumer products, ongoing profitability of cellular services and lower interest charges should improve performance in the second half of the year.</p>
<p>The purchase of AWA's electronics business in Australia would, when completed, dilute shares by about four percent but there would be no material effect on earnings per share during the current year.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
